+# Exact experiment-stratum pair contract
+
+This contract prevents reward-model pairs from comparing candidates produced under different
+execution configurations. A structure-only audit of the 2026-08-18 augmented snapshot found 708
+such pairs among 9,001 full-train pairs. All 708 shared the same parsed run family and date, which
+is consistent with mixed configurations inside directories assumed to be homogeneous.
+
+## Contract v1
+
+Before shuffling or applying the per-task cap, candidate nodes are partitioned by the exact tuple:
+
+```text
+(task.name, client, hardware, time_limit, execution_timeout)
+```
+
+Only nodes in the same partition may form a pair. The existing cap remains per task, so this patch
+does not increase the number of sampled pairs merely because a task has multiple strata. A physical
+run containing more than one tuple fails closed.
+
+Every emitted pair carries two receipts:
+
+- `experiment_stratum_sha256`: SHA256 of the canonical JSON tuple above;
+- `batch_cards_sha256`: byte-level SHA256 of the `batch_cards.json` input.
+
+`build_batch_value_pairs.sh` invokes an independent verifier before concatenation. The verifier
+recomputes both hashes without importing the pair producer, rejects unknown/duplicate endpoints and
+cross-stratum pairs, scans inputs for credential-shaped bytes before JSON parsing, and writes a
+per-batch `batch_value_pairs_receipt.json`.
+
+## Migration boundary
+
+This patch is future-only. Rebuilding or filtering an already inspected pair file does not convert
+old scaling results into a confirmatory evaluation. A new cohort should be built under this contract,
+receive a train-only physical-run dev split, select checkpoints on dev, and touch frozen test once.
+
+The six new focused contract/verifier tests pass. At source commit
+`92a9651f2e13a9e43623235b82c07c19721bc2ee`, the pre-existing subtree-pair test file already has five
+failures and one pass; the same five legacy failures remain after this patch and concern node-value
+eligibility expectations outside the experiment-stratum change.
